      "body": "## Motivation\n\nPoint fix for #43287 (kept open for the structural question). With EAGLE + DP attention + triton and an eager idle verify, the idle rank crashes with `AttributeError: 'EagleVerifyInput' object has no attribute 'kv_indptr'`. Root cause, repro and trigger conditions are in the issue.\n\n**Draft on purpose:** this is the second time the same failure has shown up in a `SpecInput` subclass (see #28221). The issue asks maintainers whether they prefer a structural fix, such as declaring the fields on `SpecInput`, gating the backend reads, or decoupling the idle path from `spec_info`. I'll rework this PR into whichever direction is chosen.\n\n## Modifications\n\nDeclare `kv_indptr` / `kv_indices` as `None` on `EagleVerifyInput`, matching `EagleDraftInput`. Verify inputs never populate them. The `None` value makes the backend's existing \"rebuild plain metadata from `seq_lens`\" fallback reachable for the idle verify batch.\n\nBoth fields are needed: some paths read both (e.g. `triton_backend.py:740-741`), so declaring only one just moves the crash to the next line.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo output change: no change for non-idle verify (`TARGET_VERIFY` takes a different branch and never reads these fields) or for the CUDA-graph idle path.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A (declaration only, no hot-path change).\n\n### Repro / functional test\n\n4× GB300, Qwen3-30B-A3B + EAGLE3 draft, TP2/DP2, `--enable-dp-attention --attention-backend triton`, 6 sequential single requests. Tested on a downstream fork that shares this code path with `main`, not on `main` itself:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--disable-cuda-graph` | crash on warmup request | 6/6 OK |\n| CUDA graph on | 6/6 OK | 6/6 OK |\n\nNo CI test added yet; the issue proposes one (idle verify per backend × algorithm under DP attention, eager), pending the direction discussion.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37884569906](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37884569906)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37884569806](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37884569806)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37884569963](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37884569963)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
